# Normalise text files to LF inside the repository and check them out in each
# platform's native form.
#
# Without this the repository has drifted into a mix: the C# files and .gitignore
# were committed from Visual Studio with CRLF, while README.md, LICENSE and
# appsettings.json are LF. Editing a CRLF file from Linux (or the reverse) then
# rewrites every line, so a one line change can arrive as a two hundred line diff
# that hides what actually changed.
#
# text=auto with no eol setting is deliberate. This project is edited both in
# Visual Studio on Windows and directly on the Raspberry Pi over SSH, so pinning
# the working tree to one line ending would fight one of those. Normalising in
# the repository and checking out natively suits both.

* text=auto

# Never touch binaries. Scanned documents and screen captures pass through here.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.pdf binary
*.bin binary
*.ico binary
